# setup.env -- Runtime configuration example
#
# Location and precedence
# -----------------------
# Keep this file outside all PAK archives: it is read before archive mounting.
# The asset root is assets/ beside the executable, unless --assets selects it.
# If assets/files/ is the resource root, its setup.env is tried first; the
# outer assets/setup.env is used only when the inner file does not exist.
# File entries override process environment variables. A missing entry falls
# through to the process environment, then to that option's code default.
# Settings are cached. Restart the game after editing this file.
#
# Syntax
# ------
# Use "set NAME=value" or "NAME=value", one assignment per line.
# Comments must occupy their own line and start with # in the first column.
# Inline comments are not supported: never append "# comment" to an assignment.
# Uncomment an example by removing "# " at the beginning of its line.
# Repeated assignments use the last value. "unset NAME=" removes a file entry;
# it does not remove the process environment variable. The equals sign is
# required by the current parser. An empty assignment is not an unset.
# Save as UTF-8 without a BOM.
# Boolean true values: 1, yes, true, True.
# Boolean false values: 0, no, false, False.
# Unrecognized boolean values use the option's code default.
# Integer options require decimal numbers; malformed text may become zero.
# Single quotes preserve the contents literally. Double quotes decode escape
# sequences such as backslash-n, backslash-r, and backslash-t.
# For Windows paths, use forward slashes or single quotes to keep backslashes.
#
# Copy this file to assets/setup.env, or assets/files/setup.env when using files/.
# Uncommented assignments are this example's preferences, not necessarily code
# defaults. Commented assignments are optional; descriptions give code defaults.

# Language and resource packs
# ---------------------------
# LAWN_LANGUAGE: language pack name; default en_us when omitted or empty.
# en_us selects assets/en_us.pak; zh_cn selects assets/zh_cn.pak.
# Other languages require a matching assets/<language>.pak.
# assets/main.pak is mounted independently. Lookup priority is loose files,
# then the selected language pack, then main.pak. A missing language pack
# leaves existing resources available. This does not select a system locale.
set LAWN_LANGUAGE=en_us
# set LAWN_LANGUAGE=zh_cn

# Rendering and frame pacing
# --------------------------
# SEXY_VIDEO_DRIVER: rendering backend; default auto.
# auto: let bgfx select a supported renderer for the current platform.
# dx11 / d3d11: Direct3D 11; dx12 / d3d12: Direct3D 12 (Windows).
# gl / opengl: OpenGL; vk / vulkan: Vulkan; metal: Metal (Apple platforms).
# bgfx is an alias for auto. An unavailable requested renderer or missing
# shaders causes an initialization error.
# software / sw selects the legacy software backend; it has limited rendering
# support and is intended for diagnosis rather than normal gameplay.
# GPU shader packages must be supplied in assets/shaders/.
set SEXY_VIDEO_DRIVER=auto

# SEXY_BGFX_DEBUG: enable bgfx GPU validation/debugging; default 0.
# Independent of the C++ Debug/Release build configuration. Requires platform
# support and may add driver/debugger overhead.
set SEXY_BGFX_DEBUG=0

# SEXY_BGFX_PROFILE: enable bgfx GPU profiling markers; default 0.
# Independent of the C++ build configuration; may add profiling overhead.
set SEXY_BGFX_PROFILE=0

# SEXY_MAX_FPS: callback/frame limit in frames per second; default 60.
# Use a positive integer for a limit; 0 removes the normal frame cap.
# The intro video runs at 30 FPS. Game updates advance with rendered frames,
# so changing this value can change gameplay speed.
set SEXY_MAX_FPS=60

# LAWN_NO_INTRO_VIDEO: skip the startup movie; default 0.
# 0 plays movies/intro.mpg (MPEG-1, including audio); 1 skips it.
# The original MPEG-4 intro.mp4 is not the file used by this playback path.
set LAWN_NO_INTRO_VIDEO=1

# Gameplay and camera
# -------------------
# LAWN_AUTO_COLLECT: automatically collect ordinary sun, coins, diamonds,
# and Versus brains using their existing pickup delays/animations; default 0.
# Cooperative sun retains its two-player pickup rules. Final seed-packet
# rewards still require manual collection.
set LAWN_AUTO_COLLECT=1

# LAWN_HIDE_COVER_LAYER: hide right-side bushes, foreground cover, and the
# roof tree/pole; default 0. This changes visibility, not gameplay rules.
set LAWN_HIDE_COVER_LAYER=1

# LAWN_LOW_VIEW: PC-style low camera in lawn stages; default 0 (TV camera).
# 1 uniformly scales the lawn to the 720-high logical canvas. Window aspect
# ratio determines the visible horizontal range.
# Single-player uses the larger PC-style seed bank and tools. The bank,
# visible tools, and menu form one horizontally centered group at the top edge;
# the menu moves below the bank when the full row does not fit.
# Ready flashes, tutorial arrows, hit-testing, and gamepad selection animations
# follow the bank. Two-player modes retain the TV dual-bank layout.
# Zen Garden, Tree of Wisdom, intro, and upsell scenes keep their original view.
set LAWN_LOW_VIEW=0

# Input
# -----
# LAWN_GAMEPAD_MODE: enable gamepad-aware UI behavior; default 1.
# With 1, available SDL gamepads can be recognized by the game UI, and button
# tags such as <A> can display controller glyphs. Detection supports hotplugging.
# 0 suppresses these glyphs and the application's HasGamepad result; it does
# not switch off SDL's physical controller event delivery.
# set LAWN_GAMEPAD_MODE=1

# LAWN_SIMULATE_GAMEPAD: legacy simulated-gamepad UI flag; default 0.
# 1 permits UI branches that accept simulation when LAWN_GAMEPAD_MODE is also 1.
# This flag does not create an SDL controller or install custom key mappings.
# LAWN_BUTTON_MAP is not read by the current implementation.
# set LAWN_SIMULATE_GAMEPAD=0

# SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG_FILE: optional SDL controller mapping database.
# Defaults to gamecontrollerdb.txt in the asset root if that file exists.
# Accepts an absolute path or a path relative to the asset root.
# Existing SDL mappings take priority over generated generic HID mappings.
# set SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG_FILE=gamecontrollerdb.txt

# SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG: optional SDL-format controller mapping string.
# Use SDL's official GUID,name,button/axis mapping syntax for the device.
# This is separate from the mapping database file.
# set SDL_GAMECONTROLLERCONFIG='GUID,Controller Name,a:b0,b:b1,x:b2,y:b3,'

# SEXY_NO_DRAG: suppress mouse-drag dispatch while a button is held; default 0.
# 1 can interfere with dragging seed packets, lists, and other mouse controls.
# set SEXY_NO_DRAG=0

# Resource loading and music
# --------------------------
# SEXY_LOADING_THREAD: execute resource-loading work on a background thread.
# Code default: 0, which processes one loading slice per frame on the main
# thread. Set to 1 to use the resource-loading worker.
# set SEXY_LOADING_THREAD=0

# SEXY_NO_THREADED_PRELOAD: suppress creation of the framework preload widget;
# default 0. This is separate from SEXY_LOADING_THREAD and does not enable or
# disable the resource-loading worker itself.
# set SEXY_NO_THREADED_PRELOAD=0

# LAWN_SAFE_RELOAD: use the game's safe image/resource reload path; default 1.
# LawnApp assigns this after the framework's SEXY_SAFE_RELOAD setting, so
# LAWN_SAFE_RELOAD determines the final value for this game.
# set LAWN_SAFE_RELOAD=1

# SEXY_SAFE_RELOAD: framework safe-reload flag; framework default 0.
# Overridden by LAWN_SAFE_RELOAD in LawnApp. Prefer the LAWN setting above.
# set SEXY_SAFE_RELOAD=0

# LAWN_MUSIC2: choose the alternate music implementation; default 0.
# 0 uses XM music with the existing layered drum/hi-hat tracks.
# 1 uses per-track OGG music and requires the corresponding audio resources.
# set LAWN_MUSIC2=0

# LAWN_NO_ATLAS: skip sprite-atlas maps and load individual images; default 0.
# 1 requires a complete set of individual image resources.
# set LAWN_NO_ATLAS=0

# Diagnostics
# -----------
# SEXY_DEBUG_DRAW_STRING: draw a rectangle around each Graphics::DrawString
# result using the font's ascent, height, and measured width; default 0.
# The flag is cached on its first use.
# set SEXY_DEBUG_DRAW_STRING=0

# SEXY_LOG: legacy framework listener specification; default default.
# The registry recognizes default, stdout, file/file://, tcp/tcp://, and
# udp/udp:// entries, separated by semicolons. Listener implementations are
# incomplete; this setting does not configure SDL_Log or publisher metrics.
# The singleton reads its initial specification before setup.env is available.
# To supply an initial value, set SEXY_LOG in the process environment before
# launch; a later explicit listener reset may read a file value.
# set SEXY_LOG=default

# SEXY_LOG_LEVEL: legacy framework verbosity table; default numeric level 1.
# Accepts a number or space-separated tag:level pairs; *:level sets the default.
# Example: '*:1 ResourceManager:0'. The singleton reads this table before
# setup.env is available, so set the process environment before launch to
# affect its initial value. This is not an SDL_Log severity configuration.
# set SEXY_LOG_LEVEL=1

# Debug shortcuts are command-line options, not setup.env settings.
# Launch LawnTV.exe -tod or LawnTV.exe --debug-keys (Debug and Release).
# Main menu: lowercase u unlocks Adventure, modes, and all 12 achievements,
# then saves the current profile. During gameplay: lowercase l opens level skip.
